    {
      "text": "A mushroom grown larger than the host’s body controls Parasect. It scatters poisonous spores.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "The larger the mushroom on its back grows, the stronger the mushroom spores it scatters.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Parasect is known to infest large trees en masse and drain nutrients from the lower trunk and roots. When an infested tree dies, they move onto another tree all at once.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Parasect is known to infest large trees en masse and drain nutrients from the lower trunk and roots. When an infested tree dies, they move onto another tree all at once.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "The large mushroom on its back controls it. It often fights over territory with Shiinotic.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It scatters toxic spores from its mushroom cap. Once harvested, these spores can be steeped and boiled down to prepare herbal medicines.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bug is mostly dead, with the mushroom on its back having become the main body. If the mushroom comes off, the bug stops moving.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its poisonous spores are also used in traditional medicine. Apparently, spores produced in Alola are not of very good quality.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bug host is drained of energy by the mushroom on its back. The mushroom appears to do all the thinking.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "The bug host is drained of energy by the mushroom on its back. The mushroom appears to do all the thinking.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mushroom-lacking specimens of this Pokémon lie unmoving in the forest, lending credence to the hypothesis that the large mushroom is in control of Parasect's actions.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
